WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:04.137
This is "Late Night."

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.604
We hope everyone's
doing well tonight

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:07.607
and I cannot stress enough
to everybody here

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.275
this is an office building.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.676
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.645
People are trying
to get work done.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:16.849
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.251
Let's get to the news.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.718
During his rally
over the weekend,

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.320
former President Trump endorsed

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.522
88-year-old
Senator Chuck Grassley

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:24.623
for reelection.

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:26.926
"Who the hell is
Chuck Grassley?"

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.661
said Chuck Grassley.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.797
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.465
Today was
Indigenous Peoples' Day.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.468
Now, of course, some people
still call it Columbus Day

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.735
and, to those people, I say,

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:38.070
how you getting back to Jersey?

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.872
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.941
PATH train?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.944
In her new book,
ex-White House Press Secretary
Stephanie Grisham

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.813
called Republican
Senator Lindsey Graham

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.582
"Senator Freeloader,"
as opposed to Trump,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.150
who doesn't call him at all.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.385
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.587
In a new interview --
Well, you know...

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:58.625
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:01.094
In a new interview,
the CEO of Airbnb said

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.295
that the largest risk
to Big Tech is

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.431
that "the world is rooting
against them."

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.101
Luckily, they can't hear it
from space.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.769
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.937
According to a new report,
the Saudi royal family

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:14.707
gave former President Trump
three robes made

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.743
with white tiger and cheetah fur

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.143
that turned out to be fake.

00:01:18.143 --> 00:01:20.146
Come on, you guys,
even Trump knows

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.215
that cheetahs
don't look like this --

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.284
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.519
The Katmai National Park
in Alaska

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.957
recently concluded online voting
in its so-called Fat Bear Week

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:34.827
and a 25-year-old bear named
Otis won for the fourth time.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:35.995
Or, more accurately,

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.897
a bear in Alaska
is being cyberbullied.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.269
"Congratulations, Otis."

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.938
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:48.874
According to a new survey,
20% of Americans say

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:51.410
they have pretended
to be bad at a task

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.979
so they wouldn't have
to do it again.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.648
So maybe that's
what the Mets are up to.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.083
One for the crew.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.351
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.552
Not going to forget you guys.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.386
You were there for me
during the lean times.

00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:04.591
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
The Boston Marathon
was held today.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.095
It's the only marathon that
starts with someone yelling --

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.329
[ Boston accent ]
Cops are here!

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:14.534
[ Cheer, laughter,
and applause ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.169
And, finally,
two men from the Soloman Islands

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.204
were recently rescued

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.140
after spending 29 days
lost at sea,

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.177
living off only oranges,
coconuts, rain water,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.478
and the third guy.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.279
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:28.581
Oh.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:32.285
Oh, Ian, oh, Ian's so happy
the groans are back.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.454
[ Laughter ]
That's what Ian wants to hear

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.688
when he writes a joke like that.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.423
[ Laughter ]
That was a monologue!

